# Auto push after changes

When code or integration files are modified for this project:

1. After finishing the requested edits, **commit and push to `master` without waiting** for the user to say "push".
2. Include only the files relevant to the change.
3. Use a concise commit message focused on why.
4. After push, briefly tell the user the commit hash and any MakerTown re-paste / cache version notes.

Do not push unrelated untracked assets (csv, modify/, node_modules, etc.).
